{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world","id":1387673,"title":"University degrees in The World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T02:50:19-07:00","id":1387673,"title":"University degrees in The World","content":"Just for fun I am brainstorming what different types of scientific disciplines there would be in The World that do not exist in real life and presenting them as a study counselor at university would.<br /> <br /> Theology<br /> This is required study for any priest of any kind that wishes to have an official clerical license. As opposed to Religious Studies which is a theoretical academic field, Theology is the study of practical applications of divine sorcery, encompassing diverse subjects such as conversation therapy to ascertain the health of the person's soul, immaculate knowledge of best practices for rituals, ceremonies and sacrifices as well as temple dogma and religious law. Theologists almost always become priests after graduation and some go on into academica. Almost no one experiences difficulty finding jobs anywhere they might go. A minor in Theology is a good investment for many other types of studies, such as lawyers, performers, technologists and psychologists.<br /> <br /> Divination<br /> Divination has always been a solid choice for the mathematically minded students. This field of study deals first and foremost with the divination of a person's traits and personality (often called Astrology) as well as estimating how the future will turn out (sometimes called Zodiology or Horoscopology). It is, however, not an easy study as it not only requires great mathematical skills but also occult understanding and the ability to make intuitive leaps to know what is or is not a valid estimation of the future. AI is projected to be able to crunch the heavy numbers involved but Diviners themselves are still in needed and in very high demand all across the labor market. Middling Diviners can still count on comfortable jobs in the corporate world while high-end Diviners look forward to high positions in governments and big corporations.<br /> <br /> Thanatology<br /> More known for the old term Necromancy (which is considered as a demeaning and outdated term), Thanatology is the study of ghosts, the underworld, ectoplasm and the afterlife in general. It is a niche field of study which sometimes experiences highs and lows in popularity. Thanatologists are by necessity investigative types who research family histories and consult with the spirits of the deceased to find the most efficient way to appease, release or, in worst case, exorcise the spirit. Thanatology majors can expect a labor market currently in balance with plenty of job opportunities.<br /> <br /> Geometry<br /> The old term Geomancy has been commonly phased out in many universities but the same principles apply: using mathematical models to calculate the flow of energy in a room or across for maximum effect. Beginners courses in Geometry are required for architecture students as well as designers. It is also an appreciated minor for many professions such as farmers, business majors, therapists or even IT-specialists. Geometricians are highly valued almost anywhere and can look forward to good career opportunities. The prerequisites are high with a solid grasp of mathematical and scientific principles necessary.<br /> <br /> Thaumatology<br /> This is still a very popular field of study in many universities but job opportunities are unfortunately slim as sorcery is not as popular as it was a century or even 50 years ago. Many sorcery disciplines are based on ethically problematic practices such as blood sacrifice, manipulation of a person's destiny or even outright siphoning of divine energies. What's worse is that even if effective, many studies have shown that even accomplished sorcerers are prone to have fatal backfires and unforeseen consequences which has caused many countries and insurance companies to heavily regulate the use of sorcery. Many actors in the corporate world prefer the reproducibility, usability and generally much lower risk of technology for most tasks where sorcerers used to work. An undergraduate is therefore advised to consider technological disciplines instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 05-12-2020, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T05:26:43-07:00","id":1387688,"title":"","content":"I like your approach. All the possibilities are reasonable and very interesting.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would make Thaumatology more predictable after a few centuries of university studies, like Alquemy becoming chemistry, becoming less trial and error and more scientific method, the methods make magic more predictable and with more stable bad results. Also the applications of magic as a tool in many areas is great.<br /> <br /> There is a comic book called Arrowsmith ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowsmith_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowsmith_(comics)</a> ) that have a few examples of how a world with high magic would deal with it after a methodical and widespread study of magic. There are technical magic uses (like construction specialists, but for magic), while others have a more complete study of practical magic (like engineers) or magical theories and magical development (like mathematics and physics scientists).<br /> <br /> Also, one that I don\u2019t read in years, but like the concept, Shadowrun have great ideas on how humanity would deal with magic in a modern world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T06:11:37-07:00","id":1387692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387688#post1387688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your approach. All the possibilities are reasonable and very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387688#post1387688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would make Thaumatology more predictable after a few centuries of university studies, like Alquemy becoming chemistry, becoming less trial and error and more scientific method, the methods make magic more predictable and with more stable bad results. Also the applications of magic as a tool in many areas is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are of course right. I just wanted some reasons, however tenuous, for why sorcery is not more widely spread because I don't want it to be an everyday thing that every corporation would have, since it would tax my imagination and worldbuilding skills quite a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387688#post1387688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a comic book called Arrowsmith ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowsmith_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowsmith_(comics)</a> ) that have a few examples of how a world with high magic would deal with it after a methodical and widespread study of magic. There are technical magic uses (like construction specialists, but for magic), while others have a more complete study of practical magic (like engineers) or magical theories and magical development (like mathematics and physics scientists).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I will check it out!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387688#post1387688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one that I don\u2019t read in years, but like the concept, Shadowrun have great ideas on how humanity would deal with magic in a modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have purposely ignored Shadowrun because the setting does not appeal to me at all, but if it can be mined for ideas then maybe it's worth it to procure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:31:04-07:00","id":1387714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387692#post1387692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted some reasons, however tenuous, for why sorcery is not more widely spread because I don't want it to be an everyday thing that every corporation would have, since it would tax my imagination and worldbuilding skills quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point and agree completely. That\u2019s why I try to keep magic out of university, or at least out of mundane hands.<br /> <br /> An option for adding some magic without changing much the world is to make it part of the technology. You can go for a more reasonable way, where magic was studied and it\u2019s part of what we call science now (not super science, just science), so what was divination become part of statistics and chaos theory, what was alquemy become chemistry, some magical effects become quantum theory. So while not \u201cmagical\u201d leds work what was magic.<br /> The most advanced magic is still arcane in all ways, and keep it that way to give the magical effect, and it\u2019s not teached in university for ethical reasons, like human sacrifices and going against the gods will (or things like that).<br /> <br /> A second option is more akin to Avatar Legend of Kora technology, but magic instead of elemental bending. For example, an electrical generator, instead of running on fuel, has an electricity elemental locked in it, that produces energy, and computers have spirits that effectively make them work as they do for us, WiFi is based on telepathy and things like that. It keeps the world magical, but still close to our world in many ways. This one is quite silly, but still an option...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:51:08-07:00","id":1387789,"title":"","content":"Why not have two levels of magic? Cantrips are small scale things, but shrewdly used useful for daily chores and tech, and Sorcery is the high magic. Both take talent, but Sorcery takes more talent. Cantrips are slow and generally fairly weak, Sorcery is often faster and and far more powerful. The talent needed for Cantrips is moderately common. The talent needed for Sorcery is very rare and like the talent for making new tunes, you've got it or you don't.<br /> <br /> Those that can work Cantrips are common enough that Cantrips are regularly studied at universities. The Sorcery talent is rare enough for acedemic studies not to be able to get to scientific analysis. The sample is too small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-13-2020, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:03:43-07:00","id":1387804,"title":"","content":"Good idea. This way you keep magic available and studied, while truly powerful magic is still dangerous and out of reach of regular people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:53:01-07:00","id":1387887,"title":"","content":"&quot;Yeah, I got a Bachelors of Science in Metaphysics with a minor in Denizen Studies from NYU. I was going to major in Experimental Theology but I couldn't pass Omens 101 after taking it three times. Now I'm pursuing a Masters in Cthonicology&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:10:38-07:00","id":1387890,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s getting too close to a Hogwarts student checking if his OWLS are enough for Taumatology in Cambridge, after years not allowed to study it as an \u201cDark Art\u201d...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:15:02-07:00","id":1387922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387887#post1387887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Yeah, I got a Bachelors of Science in Metaphysics with a minor in Denizen Studies from NYU. I was going to major in Experimental Theology but I couldn't pass Omens 101 after taking it three times. Now I'm pursuing a Masters in Cthonicology&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a rip-off of East Texas University but in the Scion setting, could be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:15:44-07:00","id":1387923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387890#post1387890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s getting too close to a Hogwarts student checking if his OWLS are enough for Taumatology in Cambridge, after years not allowed to study it as an \u201cDark Art\u201d...</div> </div> </div> </div>You make it sound as if this is a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:18:55-07:00","id":1387926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387789#post1387789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not have two levels of magic? Cantrips are small scale things, but shrewdly used useful for daily chores and tech, and Sorcery is the high magic. Both take talent, but Sorcery takes more talent. Cantrips are slow and generally fairly weak, Sorcery is often faster and and far more powerful. The talent needed for Cantrips is moderately common. The talent needed for Sorcery is very rare and like the talent for making new tunes, you've got it or you don't.<br /> <br /> Those that can work Cantrips are common enough that Cantrips are regularly studied at universities. The Sorcery talent is rare enough for acedemic studies not to be able to get to scientific analysis. The sample is too small.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent idea, I shall consider it. Really, I would personally base sorcery in The World on real life folklore magic and so Cantrips are simpler magic tricks that can work if done properly, such as putting glass in the footprints of a person to hurt them. Meanwhile Sorcery is the blatant siphoning of divine energies, human sacrifices and similar taboo subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:17:35-07:00","id":1387941,"title":"","content":"Some more fun university degrees, this time Master Degrees:<br /> <br /> Eschatology Master's Degree<br /> The name has inspired many jokes among first year students, but students of this discipline take it highly seriously. Eschatologists study all the catastrophes, omens, apocalypses and so on that are present in all religions and try to verify if such events are coming to pass or no. That hail storm in the middle of summer is usually just a freak meteorological phenomenon, but it might just be a sign of some coming apocalypse or catastrophe on the way if all the conditions are true. Forewarned is forearmed and some governments value the counsel of Eschatologists but just as many do not. As such, a Masters degree in Eschatology is not a surefire road to safe employment. Eschatology students almost always have a background in Religious Studies but History and Theology are also common.<br /> <br /> Enochian Studies Master's Degree<br /> This is the study of enochian spirit magic as well as angel hierarchies and categories of celestial beings. It claims a long tradition from early Christian Angelology and the principles set forth by John Dee but the modern formalised version is much more recent. Some accuse this of being more of a Judeo-Christian sect than a Master's Degree as it places a lot of importance into the power of angelic beings and the potential benefits of supplicating and appeasing them. Many also proclaim that the appearances and utterances of angels signify great events and omens. Some Enochian students also claim to have mastery of Enochian, the supposed language of Angels.<br /> <br /> Animology Master's Degree<br /> Sometimes called Neurotheology, sometimes Animancy. This is the study of the soul and all aspects of it. It is a highly interdisciplinary study encompassing everything from concrete neurology to philosophy. The goal of most animologists is to find scientific and accurate ways to gauge the health of a person's soul in order to prescribe the most effective spiritual remedies. Many mock these attempts and ambitions as it is commonly taken for granted that priests of various religions already have this knowledge and the answers. The ambitions of animologists however would be to seek the underpinnings of the soul and how sin works on it as well as to more effectively find spiritual remedies and separate the fact from fiction across religious dogmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 05-13-2020, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:36:15-07:00","id":1388018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1387923#post1387923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You make it sound as if this is a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definetly it\u2019s not bad. I love the idea! I like Harry Potter a lot and, while HP don\u2019t fit exactly on Scion, I do enjoy bringing things from one setting to the other. Actually it\u2019s weird to me that there is no Wizard University in Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> One question: What would you think would be the reaction of gods to be studied, or having their domain studied? For example, hades don\u2019t like Necromancy as it goes against his domain (trying to bring souls from his domain is on the list of things he kills for).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-13-2020, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:12:11-07:00","id":1388050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387673-university-degrees-in-the-world?p=1388018#post1388018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question: What would you think would be the reaction of gods to be studied, or having their domain studied? For example, hades don\u2019t like Necromancy as it goes against his domain (trying to bring souls from his domain is on the list of things he kills for).</div> </div> </div> </div>In my personal vision of The World the gods are far too busy fighting Titans and engaging in divine politics to care one bit about the silly science of mortals. The priests of the gods, however, are a different story altogether and they might well criticise, condemn or even assault scientists for all sorts of slights they perceive against their religions and gods. In fact, that would be a good source for plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}